IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-eligibility`

-- Old Age Security Act, PART II, sections 13 and 14: how income is calculated for a month before July 1, 1999, and
-- the statement or estimate of income that goes with an application. Piece oa2.
--
-- Section 2's definition of "income" (the current one) is the keel's `the income of a person for a calendar year`;
-- section 13 is its older twin, for months before July 1, 1999, with a different list of deductions, and is encoded
-- here as its own record and rules (the keel's `Income facts` lacks two of section 13's items).
-- Section 14 is about statements. The Minister's powers are BOOLEAN rules over the facts the Act names; the amounts
-- of the estimates are NUMBER rules. Every judgment the Act leaves to the Minister is a fact the caller states.

§ `Part II -- Monthly Guaranteed Income Supplement`

§§ `Calculation of income, section 13`

-- The figures for one person and one calendar year that section 13 reads. "the person's or applicant's income": one
-- record is made for the person whose income it is (the applicant, or the spouse or common-law partner).
DECLARE `s 13: Income facts` HAS
    `income for the year computed in accordance with the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER     -- out of range: Income Tax Act (no piece; a plain input)
    `income from office or employment for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `employee's premiums paid during the year under the Employment Insurance Act` IS A NUMBER
    `employee's contributions made during the year under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
    `self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
    `contributions made in respect of those self-employed earnings under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
    `premium paid during the year under Part VII.1 of the Employment Insurance Act` IS A NUMBER
    `benefits under this Act and similar payments under a law of a provincial legislature, included in the income` IS A NUMBER
    `allowances under the Family Allowances Act and similar payments under a law of a provincial legislature, included in the income` IS A NUMBER
    `death benefits under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan, included in the income` IS A NUMBER
    `grants under a prescribed home insulation or energy conversion program of the Government of Canada, included in the income` IS A NUMBER     -- out of range: the program is prescribed, and the Old Age Security Regulations do not name it (no piece; a plain input)
    `social assistance payments described in subparagraph 13(c)(v), included in the income` IS A NUMBER

-- (a)(i) "a single amount in respect of all offices and employments ... equal to the lesser of five hundred dollars
-- and one fifth of the person's or applicant's income from office or employment for that year"
-- src:365 | (i) a single amount in respect of all offices and employments of that person or applicant equal to the lesser of five hundred dollars and one fifth of the person’s or applicant’s income from office or employment for that year,
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 13(a)(i) (src:365)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 13: Income facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 13(a)(i): the single amount deducted` facts MEANS
    min 500 ((facts's `income from office or employment for the year`) DIVIDED BY 5)

-- (a): the three deductions from income from office or employment: (i) the single amount, (ii) the Employment
-- Insurance premiums and (iii) the Canada Pension Plan contributions.
-- src:364 | (a) there shall be deducted from the person’s or applicant’s income from office or employment for that year
-- src:365 | (i) a single amount in respect of all offices and employments of that person or applicant equal to the lesser of five hundred dollars and one fifth of the person’s or applicant’s income from office or employment for that year,
-- src:366 | (ii) the amount of employee’s premiums paid by the person or applicant during the year under the Employment Insurance Act, and
-- src:367 | (iii) the amount of employee’s contributions made by the person or applicant during the year under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan as defined in section 3 of that Act;
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 13(a) (src:364-367)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 13: Income facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 13(a): the deduction from income from office or employment` facts MEANS
        `s 13(a)(i): the single amount deducted` facts
    PLUS facts's `employee's premiums paid during the year under the Employment Insurance Act`
    PLUS facts's `employee's contributions made during the year under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan`

-- (b): from the self-employed earnings, (i) the contributions made in respect of them under the Canada Pension Plan
-- or a provincial pension plan and (ii) the premium paid under Part VII.1 of the Employment Insurance Act.
-- src:368 | (b) there shall be deducted from the person’s or applicant’s self-employed earnings for that year
-- src:369 | (i) the amount of contributions made in respect of those self-employed earnings by the person or applicant during the year under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan as defined in section 3 of that Act, and
-- src:370 | (ii) the amount of premium paid by the person or applicant during the year under Part VII.1 of the Employment Insurance Act; and
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 13(b) (src:368-370)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 13: Income facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 13(b): the deduction from self-employed earnings` facts MEANS
        facts's `contributions made in respect of those self-employed earnings under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan`
    PLUS facts's `premium paid during the year under Part VII.1 of the Employment Insurance Act`

-- (c): the five kinds of amount, "to the extent that those amounts have been included in computing that income".
-- src:371 | (c) there shall be deducted from the person’s or applicant’s income for that year, to the extent that those amounts have been included in computing that income,
-- src:372 | (i) the amount of any benefit under this Act and the amount of any similar payment under a law of a provincial legislature,
-- src:373 | (ii) the amount of any allowance under the Family Allowances Act and the amount of any similar payment under a law of a provincial legislature,
-- src:374 | (iii) the amount of any death benefit under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan as defined in section 3 of that Act,
-- src:375 | (iv) the amount of any grant under a program that is a prescribed program of the Government of Canada relating to home insulation or energy conversion for the purposes of paragraphs 12(1)(u) and 56(1)(s) of the Income Tax Act, and
-- src:376 | (v) the amount of any social assistance payment made on the basis of a means, a needs or an income test by a registered charity as defined in subsection 248(1) of the Income Tax Act or under a program provided for by an Act of Parliament or a provincial legislature that is neither a program prescribed under the Income Tax Act nor a program under which the amounts referred to in subparagraph (i) are paid.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 13(c) (src:371-376)
GIVEN facts IS A `s 13: Income facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 13(c): the deduction from income` facts MEANS
        facts's `benefits under this Act and similar payments under a law of a provincial legislature, included in the income`
    PLUS facts's `allowances under the Family Allowances Act and similar payments under a law of a provincial legislature, included in the income`
    PLUS facts's `death benefits under the Canada Pension Plan or a provincial pension plan, included in the income`
    PLUS facts's `grants under a prescribed home insulation or energy conversion program of the Government of Canada, included in the income`
    PLUS facts's `social assistance payments described in subparagraph 13(c)(v), included in the income`

-- The lead-in: "For the purposes of determining the amount of supplement that may be paid to a pensioner for a month
-- before July 1, 1999, the income for a calendar year of a person or an applicant is the income of that person or
-- applicant for that year computed in accordance with the Income Tax Act, except that" the three sets of deductions
-- are made. For a month on or after July 1, 1999 section 13 does not speak (section 2's definition does): NOTHING.
-- The result is not limited to zero: the section says nothing of the kind.
-- src:363 | 13 For the purposes of determining the amount of supplement that may be paid to a pensioner for a month before July 1, 1999, the income for a calendar year of a person or an applicant is the income of that person or applicant for that year computed in accordance with the Income Tax Act, except that
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 13 (src:363)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      facts IS A `s 13: Income facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 13: the income of a person for a calendar year, for a month before July 1, 1999` month facts MEANS
    IF `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN (YMD 1999 7 1)
    THEN JUST (  facts's `income for the year computed in accordance with the Income Tax Act`
               MINUS `s 13(a): the deduction from income from office or employment` facts
               MINUS `s 13(b): the deduction from self-employed earnings` facts
               MINUS `s 13(c): the deduction from income` facts)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Statement or estimate of income, section 14`

-- (1) "Every person by whom an application for a supplement in respect of a current payment period is made shall, in
-- the application, make a statement of the person's income for the base calendar year."
-- src:380 | 14 (1) Every person by whom an application for a supplement in respect of a current payment period is made shall, in the application, make a statement of the person’s income for the base calendar year.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(1) (src:380)
GIVEN `an application for a supplement in respect of a current payment period is made by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(1): the person must make a statement of the person's income for the base calendar year in the application` `an application for a supplement in respect of a current payment period is made by the person` MEANS
    `an application for a supplement in respect of a current payment period is made by the person`

-- (1.01) "The Minister may waive the requirement ... if that information has been made available to the Minister
-- under this Act and, in that case, the statement is deemed to have been made for the purposes of this Part."
-- src:382 | (1.01) The Minister may waive the requirement to make a statement of income under subsection (1) if that information has been made available to the Minister under this Act and, in that case, the statement is deemed to have been made for the purposes of this Part.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(1.01) (src:382)
GIVEN `the information has been made available to the Minister under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(1.01): the Minister may waive the requirement to make a statement of income` `the information has been made available to the Minister under this Act` MEANS
    `the information has been made available to the Minister under this Act`

-- The requirement is met when the statement is made in the application, or when the Minister has waived it (and the
-- statement is then deemed to have been made).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(1), s 14(1.01) (src:380) (src:382)
GIVEN `the statement of income is made in the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has waived the requirement to make a statement of income` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(1.01): the statement of income is made or is deemed to have been made` `the statement of income is made in the application` `the Minister has waived the requirement to make a statement of income` MEANS
    `the statement of income is made in the application` OR `the Minister has waived the requirement to make a statement of income`

-- (1.1) "If the requirement for an application for payment of a supplement for any month has been waived under
-- subsection 11(3.1) or (4), the Minister may, on the basis of the information available to him or her, (a) estimate
-- the applicant's income for the base calendar year; and (b) in the case of an applicant who is a person described
-- in subsection 15(2), estimate the income of the applicant's spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year."
-- src:384 | (1.1) If the requirement for an application for payment of a supplement for any month has been waived under subsection 11(3.1) or (4), the Minister may, on the basis of the information available to him or her,
-- src:385 | (a) estimate the applicant’s income for the base calendar year; and
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(1.1)(a) (src:384-385)
GIVEN `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(1.1)(a): the Minister may estimate the applicant's income for the base calendar year` `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(3.1)` `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(4)` MEANS
    `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(3.1)` OR `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(4)`

-- src:386 | (b) in the case of an applicant who is a person described in subsection 15(2), estimate the income of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(1.1)(b) (src:386)
GIVEN `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(3.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a person described in subsection 15(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(1.1)(b): the Minister may estimate the income of the applicant's spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(3.1)` `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(4)` `the applicant is a person described in subsection 15(2)` MEANS
        (   `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(3.1)`
         OR `the requirement for an application has been waived under subsection 11(4)`)
    AND `the applicant is a person described in subsection 15(2)`

-- (1.2) "Where a person's income for a base calendar year has been estimated under subsection (1.1), the Minister
-- may require that the person make a statement to the Minister of their income for any month in that year."
-- src:388 | (1.2) Where a person’s income for a base calendar year has been estimated under subsection (1.1), the Minister may require that the person make a statement to the Minister of their income for any month in that year.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(1.2) (src:388)
GIVEN `the person's income for the base calendar year has been estimated under subsection 14(1.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(1.2): the Minister may require the person to make a statement of the person's income for any month in that year` `the person's income for the base calendar year has been estimated under subsection 14(1.1)` MEANS
    `the person's income for the base calendar year has been estimated under subsection 14(1.1)`

-- The three figures of every estimate in subsections (2) to (6): "(a) any pension income ..., (b) the income from any
-- office or employment or any business ..., and (c) the person's income for the base calendar year calculated as
-- though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension
-- income". What counts as (a) and (b) differs by subsection and is named in each rule; the caller states the sums.
DECLARE `s 14: Figures for a statement of estimated income` HAS
    `the pension income received by the person in the period the subsection names` IS A NUMBER     -- out of range: Regulation 14, pension income (piece oa3)
    `the income from any office or employment or any business that the subsection counts` IS A NUMBER
    `the person's income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income` IS A NUMBER

-- How many months there are "in that part of that calendar year that is after the month in which the person ceases
-- ...": the months from the month after the month named up to December of its year.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(2)(a) "the number of months in that part of that calendar year" (src:391)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 14(2)(a): the number of months in the part of the calendar year that is after the month` month MEANS
    `the number of months from the month containing` month `to the month containing` (Date 1 12 (DATE_YEAR month))

-- "after the month immediately before the month in which the loss is suffered" (subsections (4)(a), (6)(b)(i)): the
-- part starts with the month of the loss itself, so it is one month longer.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(4)(a) "the number of months in that part of that calendar year" (src:401)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 14(4)(a): the number of months in the part of the calendar year that is after the month immediately before the month` month MEANS
    `s 14(2)(a): the number of months in the part of the calendar year that is after the month` month PLUS 1

-- "divided by the number of months in that part of that calendar year and multiplied by 12". A part with no months
-- (the person ceased in December, which subsection (3) deals with) cannot be divided: NOTHING.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(2)(a) "divided by ... multiplied by 12" (src:391)
GIVEN `the pension income received` IS A NUMBER     -- out of range: Regulation 14, pension income (piece oa3)
      `the number of months in the part` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 14(2)(a): the pension income divided by the number of months and multiplied by 12` `the pension income received` `the number of months in the part` MEANS
    IF `the number of months in the part` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN JUST ((`the pension income received` DIVIDED BY `the number of months in the part`) TIMES 12)
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The last day of the payment period that begins the day after the one containing the day named: the payment
-- period "immediately after" a payment period.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(2) "the second payment period after the current payment period" (src:390)
GIVEN `the current payment period` IS A `Calendar span`
GIVETH A `Calendar span`
`s 14(2): the payment period immediately after the payment period` `the current payment period` MEANS
    `the payment period in relation to the month containing` (`the day that is` (`a limit in days` 1) `after` (`the current payment period`'s `last day`))

-- (2) "not later than the end of the second payment period after the current payment period"
-- src:390 | (2) If in a current payment period a person who is an applicant, or is an applicant’s spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a), ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business, that person may, not later than the end of the second payment period after the current payment period, in addition to making the statement of income required by subsection (1) in the case of the applicant or in addition to filing a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a) in the case of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner, file a statement of the person’s estimated income for the calendar year in which the person ceased to hold that office or employment or ceased to carry on that business, which income shall be calculated as the total of
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(2) (src:390)
GIVEN `the current payment period` IS A `Calendar span`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 14(2): the last day on which the statement of estimated income may be filed` `the current payment period` MEANS
    (`s 14(2): the payment period immediately after the payment period` (`s 14(2): the payment period immediately after the payment period` `the current payment period`))'s `last day`

-- (5) and (6): "not later than the end of the payment period that is immediately after the current payment period"
-- src:405 | (5) If, in the circumstances described in paragraphs (a) and (b), a person who is an applicant, or is an applicant’s spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a), ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business, the person may, not later than the end of the payment period that is immediately after the current payment period, in addition to making the statement of income required by subsection (1) in the case of the applicant or in addition to filing a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a) in the case of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner,
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(5) (src:405)
GIVEN `the current payment period` IS A `Calendar span`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 14(5): the last day on which the statement of estimated income may be filed` `the current payment period` MEANS
    (`s 14(2): the payment period immediately after the payment period` `the current payment period`)'s `last day`

-- (3) "in the last month of a calendar year that ends in the current payment period": the month is December and is
-- in the current payment period.
-- src:395 | (3) Despite subsection (2), if in the last month of a calendar year that ends in the current payment period a person who is an applicant, or is an applicant’s spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a), ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business, the person may, not later than the end of the second payment period after the current payment period, in addition to making the statement of income required by subsection (1) in the case of the applicant or in addition to filing a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a) in the case of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner, file a statement of the person’s estimated income for the calendar year that is immediately after the month in which the person ceased to hold that office or employment or ceased to carry on that business, which income shall be calculated as the total of
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(3) (src:395)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the current payment period` IS A `Calendar span`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(3): the month is the last month of a calendar year that ends in the current payment period` month `the current payment period` MEANS
        DATE_MONTH month EQUALS 12
    AND `the first day of the month containing` month AT LEAST `the current payment period`'s `first day`
    AND `the first day of the month containing` month AT MOST `the current payment period`'s `last day`

-- (2) "If in a current payment period a person who is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law
-- partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a), ceases to hold an office or employment or
-- ceases to carry on a business, that person may, not later than the end of the second payment period after the
-- current payment period, ... file a statement of the person's estimated income". Subsection (3) applies "despite
-- subsection (2)" to a person who ceases in December, so (2) does not.
-- src:390 | (2) If in a current payment period a person who is an applicant, or is an applicant’s spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a), ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business, that person may, not later than the end of the second payment period after the current payment period, in addition to making the statement of income required by subsection (1) in the case of the applicant or in addition to filing a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a) in the case of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner, file a statement of the person’s estimated income for the calendar year in which the person ceased to hold that office or employment or ceased to carry on that business, which income shall be calculated as the total of
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(2) who may file (src:390)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` IS A DATE
      `the current payment period` IS A `Calendar span`
      `the day on which the statement is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(2): the person may file a statement of estimated income` `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)` `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` `the current payment period` `the day on which the statement is filed` MEANS
        `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)`
    AND `the first day of the month containing` `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` AT LEAST `the current payment period`'s `first day`
    AND `the first day of the month containing` `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` AT MOST `the current payment period`'s `last day`
    AND NOT `s 14(3): the month is the last month of a calendar year that ends in the current payment period` `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` `the current payment period`
    AND `the day on which the statement is filed` AT MOST `s 14(2): the last day on which the statement of estimated income may be filed` `the current payment period`

-- (2) The estimated income: the total of (a) the pension income received after the month of ceasing, annualised,
-- (b) the income from any other office, employment or business, and (c) the base-year income without those sources.
-- src:391 | (a) any pension income received by the person in that part of that calendar year that is after the month in which the person ceases to hold that office or employment or to carry on that business, divided by the number of months in that part of that calendar year and multiplied by 12,
-- src:392 | (b) the income from any office or employment or any business for that calendar year other than income from the office, employment or business that has ceased, and
-- src:393 | (c) the person’s income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(2)(a), (b), (c) (src:391-393)
GIVEN `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` IS A DATE
      figures IS A `s 14: Figures for a statement of estimated income`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 14(2): the estimated income` `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` figures MEANS
    CONSIDER annualised
    WHEN JUST a THEN JUST (a PLUS figures's `the income from any office or employment or any business that the subsection counts` PLUS figures's `the person's income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        annualised MEANS
            `s 14(2)(a): the pension income divided by the number of months and multiplied by 12`
                (figures's `the pension income received by the person in the period the subsection names`)
                (`s 14(2)(a): the number of months in the part of the calendar year that is after the month` `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business`)

-- (3) The person who ceases in the last month of a calendar year that ends in the current payment period may file,
-- not later than the end of the second payment period after the current one, a statement of the estimated income for
-- the calendar year immediately after: (a) the pension income received in that calendar year, (b) other income, (c).
-- src:395 | (3) Despite subsection (2), if in the last month of a calendar year that ends in the current payment period a person who is an applicant, or is an applicant’s spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a), ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business, the person may, not later than the end of the second payment period after the current payment period, in addition to making the statement of income required by subsection (1) in the case of the applicant or in addition to filing a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a) in the case of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner, file a statement of the person’s estimated income for the calendar year that is immediately after the month in which the person ceased to hold that office or employment or ceased to carry on that business, which income shall be calculated as the total of
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(3) who may file (src:395)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` IS A DATE
      `the current payment period` IS A `Calendar span`
      `the day on which the statement is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(3): the person may file a statement of estimated income` `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)` `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` `the current payment period` `the day on which the statement is filed` MEANS
        `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)`
    AND `s 14(3): the month is the last month of a calendar year that ends in the current payment period` `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` `the current payment period`
    AND `the day on which the statement is filed` AT MOST `s 14(2): the last day on which the statement of estimated income may be filed` `the current payment period`

-- src:396 | (a) any pension income received by the person in that calendar year,
-- src:397 | (b) the income from any office or employment or any business for that calendar year other than income from the office, employment or business that has ceased, and
-- src:398 | (c) the person’s income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(3)(a), (b), (c) (src:396-398)
GIVEN figures IS A `s 14: Figures for a statement of estimated income`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 14(3): the estimated income` figures MEANS
        figures's `the pension income received by the person in the period the subsection names`
    PLUS figures's `the income from any office or employment or any business that the subsection counts`
    PLUS figures's `the person's income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income`

-- (4) "If in a current payment period a person ... suffers a loss of income due to termination of or reduction in
-- pension income, the person may, not later than the end of the second payment period after the current payment
-- period, ... file a statement of the person's estimated income for the calendar year in which the loss is suffered".
-- src:400 | (4) If in a current payment period a person who is an applicant, or is an applicant’s spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a), suffers a loss of income due to termination of or reduction in pension income, the person may, not later than the end of the second payment period after the current payment period, in addition to making the statement of income required by subsection (1) in the case of the applicant or in addition to filing a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a) in the case of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner, file a statement of the person’s estimated income for the calendar year in which the loss is suffered, which income shall be calculated as the total of
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(4) who may file (src:400)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the loss is suffered` IS A DATE
      `the current payment period` IS A `Calendar span`
      `the day on which the statement is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(4): the person may file a statement of estimated income` `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)` `the month in which the loss is suffered` `the current payment period` `the day on which the statement is filed` MEANS
        `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)`
    AND `the first day of the month containing` `the month in which the loss is suffered` AT LEAST `the current payment period`'s `first day`
    AND `the first day of the month containing` `the month in which the loss is suffered` AT MOST `the current payment period`'s `last day`
    AND `the day on which the statement is filed` AT MOST `s 14(2): the last day on which the statement of estimated income may be filed` `the current payment period`

-- src:401 | (a) any pension income received by the person in that part of that calendar year that is after the month immediately before the month in which the loss is suffered, divided by the number of months in that part of that calendar year and multiplied by 12,
-- src:402 | (b) the income from any office or employment or any business for that calendar year, and
-- src:403 | (c) the person’s income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(4)(a), (b), (c) (src:401-403)
GIVEN `the month in which the loss is suffered` IS A DATE
      figures IS A `s 14: Figures for a statement of estimated income`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 14(4): the estimated income` `the month in which the loss is suffered` figures MEANS
    CONSIDER annualised
    WHEN JUST a THEN JUST (a PLUS figures's `the income from any office or employment or any business that the subsection counts` PLUS figures's `the person's income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        annualised MEANS
            `s 14(2)(a): the pension income divided by the number of months and multiplied by 12`
                (figures's `the pension income received by the person in the period the subsection names`)
                (`s 14(4)(a): the number of months in the part of the calendar year that is after the month immediately before the month` `the month in which the loss is suffered`)

-- (5) and (6): the two circumstances, (a) the event is in "the last calendar year ending before the payment period"
-- (the base calendar year of s 10) and (b) the event is in a month before the payment period and after that calendar
-- year (January to the month before the period begins). The statement is for "the calendar year ending in the
-- current payment period".
DECLARE `s 14(5): Circumstance of a person who ceased, or lost pension income, before the current payment period` IS ONE OF
    `s 14(5)(a): in the last calendar year ending before the payment period`
    `s 14(5)(b): in a month before the payment period and after the last calendar year ending before the payment period`
    `s 14(5): in neither circumstance`

-- src:405 | (5) If, in the circumstances described in paragraphs (a) and (b), a person who is an applicant, or is an applicant’s spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a), ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business, the person may, not later than the end of the payment period that is immediately after the current payment period, in addition to making the statement of income required by subsection (1) in the case of the applicant or in addition to filing a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a) in the case of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner,
-- src:406 | (a) if the person ceases to hold that office or employment or to carry on that business in the last calendar year ending before the payment period, file a statement of the person’s estimated income for the calendar year ending in the current payment period, which income shall be calculated as the total of
-- src:407 | (i) any pension income received by the person in that calendar year,
-- src:408 | (ii) the income from any office or employment or any business for that calendar year, other than income from the office, employment or business that has ceased, and
-- src:409 | (iii) the person’s income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income; and
-- src:410 | (b) if the person ceases to hold that office or employment or to carry on that business in a month that is before the payment period and after the last calendar year ending before the payment period, file a statement of the person’s estimated income for the calendar year ending in the current payment period, which income shall be calculated as the total of
-- src:411 | (i) any pension income received by the person in that part of that calendar year that is after the month in which the person ceases to hold that office or employment or to carry on that business, divided by the number of months in that part of that calendar year and multiplied by 12,
-- src:412 | (ii) the income from any office or employment or any business for that calendar year, other than income from the office, employment or business that has ceased, and
-- src:413 | (iii) the person’s income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(5) circumstances (src:405-413)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the current payment period` IS A `Calendar span`
GIVETH A `s 14(5): Circumstance of a person who ceased, or lost pension income, before the current payment period`
`s 14(5): the circumstance of the person who ceased` month `the current payment period` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the first day of the month containing` month AT LEAST baseYear's `first day` AND `the first day of the month containing` month AT MOST baseYear's `last day`
        THEN `s 14(5)(a): in the last calendar year ending before the payment period`
        IF `the first day of the month containing` month GREATER THAN baseYear's `last day` AND `the first day of the month containing` month LESS THAN `the current payment period`'s `first day`
        THEN `s 14(5)(b): in a month before the payment period and after the last calendar year ending before the payment period`
        OTHERWISE `s 14(5): in neither circumstance`
    WHERE
        baseYear MEANS `s 10: the base calendar year` `the current payment period`

-- src:405 | (5) If, in the circumstances described in paragraphs (a) and (b), a person who is an applicant, or is an applicant’s spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a), ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business, the person may, not later than the end of the payment period that is immediately after the current payment period, in addition to making the statement of income required by subsection (1) in the case of the applicant or in addition to filing a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a) in the case of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner,
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(5) who may file (src:405)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` IS A DATE
      `the current payment period` IS A `Calendar span`
      `the day on which the statement is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(5): the person may file a statement of estimated income` `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)` `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` `the current payment period` `the day on which the statement is filed` MEANS
        `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)`
    AND NOT (`s 14(5): the circumstance of the person who ceased` `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` `the current payment period` EQUALS `s 14(5): in neither circumstance`)
    AND `the day on which the statement is filed` AT MOST `s 14(5): the last day on which the statement of estimated income may be filed` `the current payment period`

-- (5)(a)(i)-(iii): the pension income received in the calendar year, other income, base income: the plain total.
-- (5)(b)(i)-(iii): as (2): the pension income after the month of ceasing, annualised, and the two others.
-- src:406 | (a) if the person ceases to hold that office or employment or to carry on that business in the last calendar year ending before the payment period, file a statement of the person’s estimated income for the calendar year ending in the current payment period, which income shall be calculated as the total of
-- src:407 | (i) any pension income received by the person in that calendar year,
-- src:408 | (ii) the income from any office or employment or any business for that calendar year, other than income from the office, employment or business that has ceased, and
-- src:409 | (iii) the person’s income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income; and
-- src:410 | (b) if the person ceases to hold that office or employment or to carry on that business in a month that is before the payment period and after the last calendar year ending before the payment period, file a statement of the person’s estimated income for the calendar year ending in the current payment period, which income shall be calculated as the total of
-- src:411 | (i) any pension income received by the person in that part of that calendar year that is after the month in which the person ceases to hold that office or employment or to carry on that business, divided by the number of months in that part of that calendar year and multiplied by 12,
-- src:412 | (ii) the income from any office or employment or any business for that calendar year, other than income from the office, employment or business that has ceased, and
-- src:413 | (iii) the person’s income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(5)(a) and (b) estimate (src:406-413)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 14(5): Circumstance of a person who ceased, or lost pension income, before the current payment period`
      `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` IS A DATE
      figures IS A `s 14: Figures for a statement of estimated income`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 14(5): the estimated income` circumstance `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business` figures MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `s 14(5)(a): in the last calendar year ending before the payment period` THEN JUST plainTotal
    WHEN `s 14(5)(b): in a month before the payment period and after the last calendar year ending before the payment period` THEN
        CONSIDER annualised
        WHEN JUST a THEN JUST (a PLUS otherIncome PLUS baseIncome)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `s 14(5): in neither circumstance` THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        otherIncome MEANS figures's `the income from any office or employment or any business that the subsection counts`
        baseIncome MEANS figures's `the person's income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income`
        plainTotal MEANS figures's `the pension income received by the person in the period the subsection names` PLUS otherIncome PLUS baseIncome
        annualised MEANS
            `s 14(2)(a): the pension income divided by the number of months and multiplied by 12`
                (figures's `the pension income received by the person in the period the subsection names`)
                (`s 14(2)(a): the number of months in the part of the calendar year that is after the month` `the month in which the person ceases to hold an office or employment or ceases to carry on a business`)

-- (6) the same for a loss of pension income, "not later than the end of the payment period that is immediately after
-- the current payment period".
-- src:415 | (6) If, in the circumstances described in paragraph (a) or (b), a person who is an applicant, or is an applicant’s spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a), suffers a loss of income due to a termination of or reduction in pension income, the person may, not later than the end of the payment period that is immediately after the current payment period, in addition to making the statement of income required by subsection (1) in the case of the applicant or in addition to filing a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a) in the case of the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner,
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(6) who may file (src:415)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the loss is suffered` IS A DATE
      `the current payment period` IS A `Calendar span`
      `the day on which the statement is filed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(6): the person may file a statement of estimated income` `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)` `the month in which the loss is suffered` `the current payment period` `the day on which the statement is filed` MEANS
        `the person is an applicant, or is an applicant's spouse or common-law partner who has filed a statement as described in paragraph 15(2)(a)`
    AND NOT (`s 14(5): the circumstance of the person who ceased` `the month in which the loss is suffered` `the current payment period` EQUALS `s 14(5): in neither circumstance`)
    AND `the day on which the statement is filed` AT MOST `s 14(5): the last day on which the statement of estimated income may be filed` `the current payment period`

-- src:416 | (a) if the loss is suffered in the last calendar year ending before the payment period, file a statement of the person’s estimated income for the calendar year ending in the current payment period, which income shall be calculated as the total of
-- src:417 | (i) any pension income received by the person in that calendar year,
-- src:418 | (ii) the income from any office or employment or any business for that calendar year, and
-- src:419 | (iii) the person’s income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income; and
-- src:420 | (b) if the loss is suffered in a month that is before the payment period and after the last calendar year ending before the payment period, file a statement of the person’s estimated income for the calendar year ending in the current payment period, which income shall be calculated as the total of
-- src:421 | (i) any pension income received by the person in that part of that calendar year that is after the month immediately before the month in which the loss is suffered, divided by the number of months in that part of that calendar year and multiplied by 12,
-- src:422 | (ii) the income from any office or employment or any business for that calendar year, and
-- src:423 | (iii) the person’s income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(6)(a) and (b) estimate (src:416-423)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 14(5): Circumstance of a person who ceased, or lost pension income, before the current payment period`
      `the month in which the loss is suffered` IS A DATE
      figures IS A `s 14: Figures for a statement of estimated income`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 14(6): the estimated income` circumstance `the month in which the loss is suffered` figures MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `s 14(5)(a): in the last calendar year ending before the payment period` THEN JUST plainTotal
    WHEN `s 14(5)(b): in a month before the payment period and after the last calendar year ending before the payment period` THEN
        CONSIDER annualised
        WHEN JUST a THEN JUST (a PLUS otherIncome PLUS baseIncome)
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `s 14(5): in neither circumstance` THEN NOTHING
    WHERE
        otherIncome MEANS figures's `the income from any office or employment or any business that the subsection counts`
        baseIncome MEANS figures's `the person's income for the base calendar year calculated as though, for that year, the person had no income from any office or employment or any business and no pension income`
        plainTotal MEANS figures's `the pension income received by the person in the period the subsection names` PLUS otherIncome PLUS baseIncome
        annualised MEANS
            `s 14(2)(a): the pension income divided by the number of months and multiplied by 12`
                (figures's `the pension income received by the person in the period the subsection names`)
                (`s 14(4)(a): the number of months in the part of the calendar year that is after the month immediately before the month` `the month in which the loss is suffered`)

-- (7) "Where under subsection (2), (3) or (4) a statement of estimated income is filed ..., no supplement calculated
-- on the basis of that statement may be paid to the applicant for any month in the current payment period before
-- (a) the month immediately following the month shown in the statement as the month in which ... ceased to hold the
-- office or employment or ceased to carry on the business, or (b) the month shown in the statement as the month in
-- which ... suffered the loss of income due to termination or reduction of pension income, whichever is applicable."
DECLARE `s 14(7): What the statement shows` IS ONE OF
    `s 14(7)(a): the month in which the person ceased to hold an office or employment or ceased to carry on a business`
    `s 14(7)(b): the month in which the person suffered the loss of income due to termination or reduction of pension income`

-- src:425 | (7) Where under subsection (2), (3) or (4) a statement of estimated income is filed by an applicant or an applicant’s spouse or common-law partner, no supplement calculated on the basis of that statement may be paid to the applicant for any month in the current payment period before
-- src:426 | (a) the month immediately following the month shown in the statement as the month in which the applicant or the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner, as the case may be, ceased to hold the office or employment or ceased to carry on the business, or
-- src:427 | (b) the month shown in the statement as the month in which the applicant or the applicant’s spouse or common-law partner, as the case may be, suffered the loss of income due to termination or reduction of pension income,
-- src:428 | whichever is applicable.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 14(7) (src:425-428)
GIVEN shown IS A `s 14(7): What the statement shows`
      `the month shown in the statement` IS A DATE     -- out of range: Regulation 13, the month of the loss (piece oa3)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 14(7): the first month for which a supplement calculated on the statement may be paid` shown `the month shown in the statement` MEANS
    CONSIDER shown
    WHEN `s 14(7)(a): the month in which the person ceased to hold an office or employment or ceased to carry on a business` THEN
        `the first day of the month that is` 1 `months after the month containing` `the month shown in the statement`
    WHEN `s 14(7)(b): the month in which the person suffered the loss of income due to termination or reduction of pension income` THEN
        `the first day of the month containing` `the month shown in the statement`
